## Key Performance Indicators

| Metric | Result |
|---|---:|
| Total Employees | 1,470 |
| Employees Left | 237 |
| Active Employees | 1,233 |
| Attrition Rate | 16.12% |
| Average Age | 36.92 |
| Average Monthly Income | 6,502.93 |
| Average Tenure | 7.01 years |

## Key Analysis Areas
- Overall employee attrition.
- Active employees compared with employees who left.
- Department-wise employee attrition.
- Average income of employees who left.
- Overtime-related attrition.
- Employee demographics and tenure.

## Excel Features Used
- Data cleaning and validation.
- Excel Tables and filters.
- Duplicate checking.
- Excel formulas.
- Conditional formatting.
- KPI reporting.

## Project Outcome
The analysis provides an overview of employee attrition and workforce characteristics. It demonstrates how Microsoft Excel can be used to clean, analyze, and present HR data to support data-driven decision-making.

